.TH CRYPTOGUARD-AGENT 1 "October 2026" "0.22.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cryptoguard-agent \- local Linux telemetry and explainable mining-risk assessment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cryptoguard-agent
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Collects Linux host, process, network, persistence and available sensor information.
Writes private local events. No process response actions or backend transport are enabled.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Report capabilities available to the invoking user. Does not create agent state.
.TP
.B run --mode standalone
Run with a separate child collector and private local state.
.TP
.B run --mode service
Run using the restricted systemd collector socket.
.TP
.B export
Write durable events as JSONL without deleting them. May run while the service runs.
.TP
.B replay FILE
Evaluate a complete normalized sample sequence using the deterministic risk engine.
.TP
.B validate FILE
Check event envelopes and null/status consistency. Full JSON Schema validation is separate.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --config FILE
Use the specified configuration; default /etc/cryptoguard/agent.json when present.
.TP
.B --state DIRECTORY
Override the state directory. Portable users should select a writable private directory.
.TP
.B --output FILE
Create an export/replay output file. Existing files are not overwritten.
.TP
.B --samples COUNT
Limit run to a specified number of samples, primarily for diagnostics.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/cryptoguard/agent.json
contains configuration and local policy.
.I /var/lib/cryptoguard
contains identity, spool and lifecycle state.
.SH PRIVACY
Argument values and unknown flags are discarded before IPC or persistence.
Hostname is redacted by default. Paths and remote IPs remain operational evidence.
.SH LIFECYCLE
SIGTERM and SIGINT request orderly shutdown. Remove preserves configuration and
state. Purge deletes /var/lib/cryptoguard including identity, events and exports.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Missing sensors produce null/status values. Snapshot process discovery can miss
short-lived processes. Device GPU metrics are not process GPU attribution.
This candidate has uncalibrated detection rules; see the acceptance report.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR dpkg (1)
